 "drug_rule": "Finasteride inhibits 5α-reductase, reducing dihydrotestosterone and shrinking the prostate. Terazosin is an α1-adrenergic antagonist that relaxes prostatic and vascular smooth muscle. Concurrent use can lead to excessive vasodilation, causing symptomatic hypotension, dizziness, and syncope. The risk is amplified in older adults due to reduced baroreceptor sensitivity and blunted compensatory mechanisms.\n\n###",
