 "drug_rule": "CYP1A2 inhibition by sertraline reduces valacyclovir clearance, elevating drug exposure. Caffeine is a CYP1A2 substrate; inhibition by sertraline and competition by valacyclovir can markedly increase caffeine levels. Hyponatremia is a known adverse effect of valacyclovir, and sertraline may impair renal concentration, while caffeine-induced diuresis further lowers sodium. The combination of these mechanisms overrides general safety assumptions.",
